1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,960
Alice?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,040
Alice, it's you, isn't it?

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,830
Yuujio!

4
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,160
Choose your actions carefully.

5
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:32,440
I have the right to remove up to
70 % of your life if I wish it.

6
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:36,756
And if you touch me again without my
permission, I will have your hand.

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,010
Alice.

8
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:44,080
Are you sure?

9
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,888
Because it's been a
while since you saw her.

10
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,980
Then we do what she says.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,130
For now.

12
00:00:50,213 --> 00:00:54,728
Now, we can argue our case with her after
we get inside the Central Cathedral.

13
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:56,757
Enough delays.

14
00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:00,600
Now, Elite Disciple Eugeo,
Elite Disciple Kirito,

15
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,560
you are in violation of the Taboo Index.

16
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:08,860
I will take you into custody, then
question you, then execute you.

17
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:20,970
. .

18
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:29,260
I'm not sure what I'm doing.

19
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,460
I hear a voice that calls you

20
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,728
Do you think you're a star?

21
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:59,177
I'm going to start with the.

22
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,597
Shining Sun, my diamond.

23
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,500
It's a dream of a dream?

24
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,340
It's time for me, I'll be here!

25
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:25,020
It's time for me, I'll be here!

26
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,310
I'll be here.

27
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,320
Tiese! Ronie!

28
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:17,137
Lady Knight, forgive our intrusion.

29
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:20,808
I'd like to return these to our
mentors with your permission.

30
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,380
Very well.

31
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:26,093
However, I cannot allow these
criminals to carry weapons.

32
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,880
I will look after them.

33
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:34,617
You have one minute.

34
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,347
Speak with them if you wish.

35
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,940
I'm sorry, Eugeo.

36
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:46,200
You shouldn't even be
in this mess. I should.

37
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,660
This is my fault.

38
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:48,900
I was dumb.

39
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:51,040
I acted so recklessly.

40
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:53,700
Stop it.

41
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:54,957
You're not to blame.

42
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,452
You did the right thing.

43
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:59,697
Your friend was in trouble and
you did what you could to help.

44
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,220
What happened is my fault, not yours.

45
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:07,500
You have nothing to be sorry
about. Ever. I promise.

46
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:10,557
Whatever it takes, I'll
become an Integrity Knight.

47
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,500
And then I'll be the one
to come and save you.

48
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,287
And I won't stop until I do.

49
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,880
Till then, don't give up hope.

50
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:20,700
I swear, I'll save you.

51
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:27,560
Um, I brought you some lunch.

52
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,180
Make sure to eat it before it spoils.

53
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:36,480
Thanks, Raiji.

54
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:39,620
It is time. Step away.

55
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,080
No.

56
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,140
Excuse me.

57
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:16,560
A robot!

58
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,070
Hey!

59
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,460
You're scaring her, Ichiemon!

60
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,800
What did you call this
thing just now? His name.

61
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,040
What else?

62
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:50,140
He's Ichie-mon, an electroactive
muscled operative machine, or E-mom.

63
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:55,020
He's also the first of his type, so
like, we added the Ichie at the top.

64
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,320
Ichie-mon, get it?

65
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:02,080
And what is this Ichie-mon doing on board?

66
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:07,177
I'm using it to fine-tune a program and
Higa here is giving me a hand with it.

67
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:10,025
We're lab partners again,
just like in college.

68
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,580
Good morning.

69
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,900
Morning. You sleep well?

70
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:21,400
Your problem is its balancer's
processor runs slow.

71
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,317
Can't you buy a faster chip?

72
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,417
It's not like you don't
have the budget to.

73
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,557
Yeah, but cooling and battery
drain would still be a problem.

74
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:31,177
Considering that, this is
the best that we can do.

75
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:35,495
One other option would be to tune the
EAP actuator to pick up the slack.

76
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,109
Sure, but the polymer muscles
are last gen, so there's that.

77
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:40,500
Upgrade to CNTs.

78
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,840
They'll take the strain
better and make it lighter.

79
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,257
We're in our own world over here.

80
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,634
Sorry about the noise.

81
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:50,950
That's okay.

82
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:56,280
If Kirito were here, he'd get a big
kick out of this robot of yours.

83
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:59,897
Actually, we built him because
the Commandante wanted us to.

84
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,440
Wait, Kikuoka did?

85
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:02,700
What for?

86
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:07,177
It's a neat idea, actually, but I'm not
sure how serious he is about it yet.

87
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:11,297
Ultimately, his goal is to bring Fluctlights
from the Underworld into our world.

88
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:14,917
But the catch is, they're going to
need something they can move around in.

89
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:19,140
So, wait, the plan is to
put the AIs in... That?

90
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:20,300
Not this guy.

91
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,617
He's just a prototype for data collection.

92
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:26,237
We have a second robot with onboard
AI that's way more advanced.

93
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,496
He operates a heck of a lot smoother.

94
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,980
Oh, you don't say.

95
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:33,640
I wonder what you
decided to call that one.

96
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,900
Niemon, of course! Knee-what?

97
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:40,040
Oh, right, knee means to.

98
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:44,598
Anyway, why does having onboard AI
in this other robot make it better?

99
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:52,420
For us to balance, our brains
make lots of micro-adjustments.

100
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,837
To replicate that
mechanically would take a lot

101
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,567
of tech and a bigger
body to house it all in.

102
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:03,220
Oh, so if a Fluctlight is
piloting instead of a CPU,

103
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:06,993
The robot can move more like
a human and also be smaller.

104
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:08,010
Bingo!

105
00:09:08,093 --> 00:09:12,277
And the smaller the tech inside, the
closer it can look like a human body.

106
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,960
Or so we hope.

107
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:16,734
For now, he's still a work in progress.

108
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,297
Niemon's coming along, though.

109
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,940
He's looking pretty human.

110
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,057
Well, his silhouette does, anyway.

111
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,817
And maybe one of these days
I'll get to see the damn thing.

112
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:30,380
Wait, you haven't gotten it to walk
around on its own yet, have you? What?

113
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,017
No, of course I haven't.

114
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,840
His CPU's all loaded up and ready to go,

115
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:38,880
but no one's home to work the
controls if you get my drift. Oh.

116
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,840
Hey, Asuna. Huh?

117
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,857
Have you had breakfast yet?

118
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:44,180
No, I haven't.

119
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:46,477
Then let's go down to
the cafeteria together.

120
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:50,100
I'd invite Higa, but he already
made plans with Ichiemon.

121
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,060
Bon appétit, ladies!

122
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:06,640
Back in a bit.

123
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,113
Something wrong, Asuna?

124
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,420
Oh, no, it's nothing. Come on!

125
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:57,561
We've only been here for a day and
a half, but it feels way longer.

126
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,565
Hey, how you doing over there?

127
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:01,960
I don't know.

128
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,593
This whole thing feels like a nightmare.

129
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:09,040
I keep seeing Umber's arm flying
off and Ryo screaming as he died.

130
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,582
Get that stuff out of your head.

131
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:14,782
Start thinking about what
we're going to do next.

132
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,482
I don't know what that could be.

133
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:22,020
You know, you're absolutely right.

134
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:24,657
We have to find a way to break out of this

135
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:27,564
cell and then figure out
what happened to Alice.

136
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:28,990
Yeah.

137
00:11:29,073 --> 00:11:31,621
If there's a way out of
this place, we'll find it.

138
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:36,200
I wonder, did they bring
Alice here eight years ago?

139
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,240
I don't know. Maybe.

140
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:43,820
Since you brought her up, I just
want to be sure of something.

141
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:47,420
The night that calls
herself Alice Synthesis 30,

142
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:51,948
you're positive that she's the
same Alice you're looking for?

143
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,120
Yeah, I am.

144
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:56,340
Those blue eyes, golden
hair, and that voice.

145
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,214
I'd never forget them.

146
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:01,157
But she seemed like a
totally different person.

147
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:05,277
For someone who's supposed to be your
childhood friend, she whacked you pretty good.

148
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,948
But if you want my opinion,

149
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:10,497
it could be she's under some kind
of mind control or something.

150
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:14,137
But I don't remember seeing spells
like that in any of our textbooks.

151
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:18,177
Right, but the high-ranking priests
in the church can manipulate life.

152
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:21,237
If they can do that, they can
control someone's mind, too.

153
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,360
Although,

154
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,779
if that night really is your Alice,

155
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:30,040
whose voice did I hear
two years ago in the cave?

156
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:34,620
Kirito, Eugeo, come and find me.

157
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:40,600
I am waiting at the top
of the central cathedral.

158
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,620
I will wait there for you both.

159
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,737
Right, you told me that.

160
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:52,260
When you and Selka were healing me,

161
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:55,857
you said you heard a voice and then
saw something that looked like Alice.

162
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:59,999
Yeah, she said she'd wait for us at
the top of the Central Cathedral.

163
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,620
And now we're stuck.

164
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:12,557
Hey, do you think we can access
the Stacia windows on these chains?

165
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,620
I never even thought to try that.

166
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,440
Give it a shot. Okay.

167
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,900
Whoa, it worked!

168
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:31,057
We could pull on these chains
forever and they'd never budge.

169
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:33,097
If we're going to break free of them,

170
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:37,298
we need to get our hands on a tool
or weapon that's at least Class 38.

171
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,486
Yeah, that won't do anything.

172
00:13:46,940 --> 00:13:48,517
I know what you're thinking,

173
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,377
but the only things we have
in here are a couple of beds,

174
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:52,917
water skins, and these chains.

175
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,580
A pair of chains.

176
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,237
Yeah, you're right, we got these chains.

177
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:06,180
Two of these suckers, just what we need!

178
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:07,750
What?

179
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,940
Hang on, I have a question.

180
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,077
Is your idea to use the
chains against one another?

181
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,400
It totally is.

182
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,477
These chains of ours have
the same durability level.

183
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:31,817
We'd need something with an object
control authority over 40 to break them.

184
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:35,841
But if we snap them against each
other, that should wear them down.

185
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,800
Just follow my lead, okay?

186
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,230
Uh...

187
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,880
Ready, and...

188
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:48,540
Hell yeah!

189
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:49,620
Not so loud.

190
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,471
You'll wake the guard up.

191
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,100
Let's give it another try.

192
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,060
Ready, and...

193
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:15,351
I think that knocked at least
a hundred points off my life.

194
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,797
That's a small price to pay
for freedom, wouldn't you say?

195
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,174
Things are looking up.

196
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,110
Mm-hmm.

197
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:25,860
All right, then.

198
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,320
If we do this, there's
no going back for us.

199
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:33,910
Remember,

200
00:15:33,993 --> 00:15:37,377
by breaking out of this cell and
looking for the truth about Alice,

201
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:41,280
or to find the Axiom Church and its laws.

202
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:46,473
That means from now on, there's no
time for second-guessing or hesitation.

203
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:50,201
You better make sure you're
prepared for that now.

204
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,982
Otherwise, you should stay here.

205
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,000
Yeah, I know.

206
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,180
But my mind's made up.

207
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:03,233
If I can return home with Alice, defying
the Church isn't even a question.

208
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:07,020
I'll even draw my sword
against them if I have to.

209
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:10,173
I want to make sure that night is Alice,

210
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:14,400
and if she is, I'll find a way to
change her back to the way she was.

211
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:18,801
That's the only thing that matters
to me, and nothing will stop me.

212
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:22,312
Remember what you said on that
picnic with Ronie and Tise?

213
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:26,901
There are things you should do,
even if the laws say you shouldn't.

214
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,513
I understand what you meant by that now.

215
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:31,850
All right.

216
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:41,568
You sound like you're ready, so
let's go give them some hell.

217
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,130
Sweet.

218
00:16:56,213 --> 00:16:57,857
Let's go before the guard wakes up.

219
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:58,770
Right.

220
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:08,810
No, no, no.

221
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:50,217
It doesn't look like anyone's following
us. No way. Look at that. What's up?

222
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,359
Is someone coming?

223
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:53,340
See these flowers?

224
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:56,260
I've heard of them.

225
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,400
Kirito, these are roses.

226
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:00,930
Oh, yeah.

227
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:02,860
No way!

228
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,160
They are roses.

229
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:06,597
And this place is chock full of them.

230
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:09,445
It's rare to find one,
but a whole garden full?

231
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,820
I can't believe we're standing here.

232
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:16,819
You and I actually made it
to the Central Cathedral.

233
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:19,740
Yeah, we're criminals,
not Integrity Knights.

234
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:22,197
But we're here, and
that's all that matters.

235
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:25,357
It's probably for the best that
things worked out this way.

236
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:29,237
If we had become Integrity Knights,
we might have ended up like Alice.

237
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:33,037
They could have gotten in our heads
and screwed with our memories, too.

238
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:36,460
I wonder if they do that to
all the Integrity Knights.

239
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:40,000
Do they forget everything
about who they were before?

240
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,160
Who knows?

241
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:43,570
Yeah, well,

242
00:18:43,653 --> 00:18:46,137
even if a knight's memories
got blocked somehow,

243
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:50,573
they'd at least remember their parents,
or the place where they were born.

244
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:53,327
Stuff like that's baked
into a person's soul.

245
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:57,617
It'd be impossible to swap out those
kind of details with fake ones.

246
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,940
You have a point.

247
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:02,197
Those fake memories would
likely be tenuous at best.

248
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:07,162
What if they were flying around while on
duty and came upon the place they grew up?

249
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:11,556
Once they saw it, they would know,
and all their memories would come...

250
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,130
What?

251
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:15,850
Not again.

252
